      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 Elsevier Masson SAS. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Circulatory assistance is developing as a treatment for patients with end-stage heart failure. There are two alternative devices: a univentricular circulatory assist pump, or a total artificial heart. It is used to bridge the time to transplantation and, increasingly, as a definitive alternative to a heart transplant."
      },
